            <ArticleTitle>Immunohistochemical analysis of accelerated graft atherosclerosis in cardiac transplantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>479-83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>HHT was performed between minimally genetic mismatched inbred strains of rats. There was no evidence of rejection and immunosuppressive therapy was not instituted. Immunohistochemical analysis using peroxidase conjugated monoclonal anti-rat ASMA of cardiac arterioles in which AGAS developed revealed a decreased peroxidase signal. The data suggest that modulation of actin expression in subintimal cells of cardiac arterioles may play a critical role in the pathologic development of AGAS.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
